A step-by-step guide to building a unique robot using a Raspberry Pi, Arduino, and Adafruit Huzzah. This project combines the power of these microcontrollers to create a robot that can interact with its environment.

The setup consists of an Arduino Uno, a Micro-USB Cable, and the Adafruit Huzzah library. The Arduino is powered by the Micro-USB Cable and connected to a PC. The Adafruit Huzzah library uses the Arduino to read temperature and GPIO inputs, then uses custom code to set up the sensors on the Arduino.

To build the robot frame, we will use a 1:1 scale model of the real robot. The frame will be made from a piece of wood, approximately 8.5x8.5 inches, with a thickness of 1/4 inch. The frame will hold a servo and a Robot Huzzah sensor on the back.

For communication with the computer, we will use the Adafruit ISP software. The code for the Arduino is as follows:

